<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry V the Fat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1248–1296</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Henry V of Legnica</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry V the Fat was a Silesian Piast duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legnica">Legnica</a> from 1278 and also of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Wrocław</a> from 1290. His reign was troubled by conflict with his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-glogow">Henry III of Głogów</a>, who held him captive for months. After his death his sons divided his inheritance in 1311, creating the separate duchies of Legnica, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brzeg">Brzeg</a> and Wrocław.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-v-the-fat.jpg" alt="Henry V the Fat" width="320" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henryk_V_Brzuchaty_seal_1289.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
